cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Bare-Metal Windows 11 on Apple Silicon: The AIC Gate"
abstract: >-
  A research concept and reproducibility plan for booting Windows 11 ARM64 to a
  functional desktop on Apple Silicon with no persistent EL2 hypervisor. The
  work isolates the decisive boot gate: Windows' HAL assumes an ARM GIC/GICD
  while Apple Silicon exposes the proprietary AIC, and no supported third-party
  interrupt-controller extension point exists. Includes a prior-art survey, an
  upstream code survey, a staged roadmap, pinned hardware and Windows targets,
  and a QEMU-based validation strategy.
authors:
  - name: "xorica27"
